WEBVTT

12:14.985 --> 12:16.195
Hello!

12:17.487 --> 12:19.031
You okay?

12:19.948 --> 12:22.117
Sorry, we didn't mean to startle you.

12:23.785 --> 12:27.956
We wouldn't have intruded but,
if you don't mind us saying,

12:28.040 --> 12:30.375
maybe you could slow
down and take a break.

12:31.460 --> 12:33.337
You've been at it for two hours straight.

12:33.420 --> 12:35.047
You people are spying on me.

12:35.130 --> 12:37.216
Oh, no. You just happened
to be outdoors this morning.

12:37.299 --> 12:40.677
How? Where?
Where are you watching me from?

12:40.761 --> 12:43.138
- An MQ-9 Reaper.
- A what?

12:43.805 --> 12:45.849
It's an Air Force drone. It's...

12:51.146 --> 12:52.523
I don't see anything.

12:53.106 --> 12:58.403
Yeah, no, you wouldn't really.
It's way up at 40,000 feet.

12:58.987 --> 13:00.864
It's not dangerous. It's not even armed.

13:02.282 --> 13:05.536
Sorry. Bad idea. It's leaving.

13:07.996 --> 13:11.375
Please? We'd feel so much better
if you'd hydrate.

13:11.959 --> 13:12.960
What's in it?

13:13.627 --> 13:14.670
Water.

13:14.753 --> 13:17.673
And what else? Something that's
gonna make me turn into one of you?

13:18.257 --> 13:20.717
No, we're months away
from knowing how to do that.

13:25.347 --> 13:27.307
Jarmell Gurky says it's okay.

13:27.391 --> 13:28.976
Who is Jarmell Gurky?

13:29.059 --> 13:32.187
He's a bottling line supervisor
in Winston-Salem.

13:32.271 --> 13:34.523
He was running the second shift
at the Aquafina plant

13:34.606 --> 13:36.316
when this got filled on May 8th.

13:36.900 --> 13:39.820
To the best of his knowledge,
it's just good clean water.

13:42.656 --> 13:44.908
Why are you standing in my yard talking

13:44.992 --> 13:47.536
about whatever the fuck it is
you're talking about?

13:48.495 --> 13:49.496
Who are you?

13:50.747 --> 13:52.249
Someone we thought you might like.

13:52.332 --> 13:54.501
Not so much. No.

13:54.585 --> 13:56.295
Sorry about that, Carol.

13:56.378 --> 13:59.006
Regardless, you are on the verge
of heat exhaustion,

13:59.673 --> 14:02.968
and that's the opinion
of every medical doctor on Earth.

14:04.803 --> 14:05.804
How about it?

14:37.419 --> 14:39.630
You have water in the house.
Please drink some.

14:40.631 --> 14:41.924
And maybe pace yourself.

14:44.384 --> 14:45.886
We can see we're upsetting you.

15:01.527 --> 15:02.528
Wait.

15:02.611 --> 15:03.612
Stop.

15:13.038 --> 15:14.957
You're gonna need a pickax by the way.

15:15.040 --> 15:17.000
There's a lot of volcanic rock
in that soil.

15:17.084 --> 15:21.380
Your neighbor Martin at 1204 has one
in his garage, along with a sun hat and

15:21.964 --> 15:22.965
work gloves.

15:28.303 --> 15:29.888
Wait right here. Don't move.

15:53.537 --> 15:55.163
What the hell is this?

15:56.582 --> 15:59.126
Are you supposed
to be my character Raban? Why?

15:59.751 --> 16:02.212
If we chose poorly, we apologize.

16:03.046 --> 16:04.882
We just want you to be happy.

16:05.465 --> 16:06.466
Why Raban as a woman?

16:10.929 --> 16:13.182
My original version of him was a her.

16:13.807 --> 16:15.184
But I talked myself out of it.

16:17.311 --> 16:18.979
And we never told anyone.

16:20.355 --> 16:22.816
Helen and I were the only ones who knew.

16:26.862 --> 16:28.322
So if you can't read minds--

16:28.405 --> 16:32.409
Carol, you may find this hard to believe
but yesterday

16:32.492 --> 16:36.413
was the greatest day
in the history of humanity.

16:37.122 --> 16:38.123
Helen thought so too.

16:38.207 --> 16:40.626
No. Helen is not one of you.

16:40.709 --> 16:42.794
She joined us before she passed.

16:42.878 --> 16:44.922
She's gone but all of her thoughts,

16:45.005 --> 16:46.590
her memories, they're right here.

16:49.009 --> 16:50.636
Should we tell you how much she loved you?

16:50.719 --> 16:53.430
You bunch of ghouls!

16:54.264 --> 16:58.769
You are a goddamn bunch
of grave-robbing psychopaths!

16:59.728 --> 17:02.022
You are the reason she is dead!

17:02.105 --> 17:03.690
And now you're gonna speak for her?

17:03.774 --> 17:07.402
Fuck you! Fuck every single one of you!

17:21.791 --> 17:22.960
Oh, jeez.

17:33.387 --> 17:34.388
Hello?

17:35.931 --> 17:37.558
Anybody?

17:39.685 --> 17:40.894
Is anybody there?

17:40.978 --> 17:42.771
Hello? Are you still there?

17:47.526 --> 17:48.527
Fuck.

18:26.023 --> 18:27.024
Shit.

18:29.443 --> 18:30.861
Shit.

18:43.624 --> 18:46.418
Jesus Christ! What's...

18:47.503 --> 18:48.504
Okay.

18:52.841 --> 18:55.052
What... Oh, my God, I...

18:55.135 --> 18:56.386
Hang on.

18:56.470 --> 18:58.222
Here we go. Here we go.

18:58.305 --> 19:00.349
Okay. I'm gonna bring you down.

19:00.432 --> 19:02.392
All right. Down, down, down!

19:02.476 --> 19:05.437
Shit! Sorry. Sorry.

19:06.063 --> 19:07.064
Hang on.

19:07.147 --> 19:09.525
No, no. No, no. No. What...

19:10.734 --> 19:12.069
Turn, turn, turn, turn, turn.

19:13.570 --> 19:15.572
No, no. Come on, come on.

19:15.656 --> 19:17.157
Fucking piece of shit!

19:21.411 --> 19:23.413
Down, down, down, down. Down.

19:24.790 --> 19:26.416
Goddamn it!

19:30.796 --> 19:33.257
Fuck. Come on. Fucking shit...

19:34.758 --> 19:36.093
- Carol?
- Fu--

19:37.469 --> 19:40.848
We can take it from here, if you like.

19:42.891 --> 19:45.310
I was just trying to...

19:45.394 --> 19:46.979
We know, Carol.

19:48.146 --> 19:49.147
We're all right.

19:51.358 --> 19:52.734
Thank you.

20:59.718 --> 21:01.887
Hi, Carol. How may we help you?

21:02.513 --> 21:04.348
The pirate lady can come back
if she wants.

21:04.431 --> 21:06.266
Absolutely. She'll be right over.

21:06.350 --> 21:07.476
Is there anything else we can...

21:54.439 --> 21:55.607
Carol?

21:59.027 --> 22:02.781
Was that me?
Did I make everybody freeze like that?

22:04.449 --> 22:06.285
We're affected by your emotions.

22:07.035 --> 22:08.036
The negative ones,

22:08.120 --> 22:12.040
if they're directed right at us,
they can be a little tough to take.

22:13.876 --> 22:16.461
So, how many people did I hurt just now?

22:16.545 --> 22:19.631
Oh, please. That is not how
you should look at this. Not at all.

22:20.757 --> 22:21.758
Did anybody die?

22:28.765 --> 22:29.766
How many?

22:35.230 --> 22:37.774
Worldwide? It's a few.

22:39.776 --> 22:40.903
Dozens?

22:45.324 --> 22:46.575
Hundreds?

23:58.105 --> 24:00.774
There is a quicker way
if you're open to it?

25:27.277 --> 25:30.739
The astronauts up in the space station,
are they like you?

25:32.366 --> 25:33.367
They are.

25:34.284 --> 25:35.536
They're on their way back.

25:38.080 --> 25:42.167
And everybody at the South Pole
and on nuclear submarines?

25:44.169 --> 25:46.421
Missile silos? Area 51?

25:46.505 --> 25:47.506
Yes.

25:48.799 --> 25:51.218
We made a point of reaching them early on.

25:51.969 --> 25:53.679
That's kind of the best way to do it.

25:54.596 --> 25:57.057
How many people like me
in the world did you say?

25:57.140 --> 25:58.308
Eleven others?

25:58.392 --> 26:00.602
Actually, now there are 12.

26:01.186 --> 26:05.482
There's a gentleman in Paraguay
whom we became aware of this morning.

26:06.942 --> 26:09.278
Were any of them hurt today when I...

26:11.905 --> 26:13.240
Did any of them get hurt?

26:14.116 --> 26:16.118
There was just one minor injury.

26:17.202 --> 26:19.997
Mostly there was consternation.

26:20.789 --> 26:22.124
They're okay.

26:27.796 --> 26:29.965
These 12, how many speak English?

26:30.632 --> 26:33.135
Five either as a second or third language.

26:33.218 --> 26:35.137
I want to meet those five.

26:35.220 --> 26:38.348
Communication wouldn't be an issue
for the 13 of you.

26:38.432 --> 26:39.933
- We can translate.
- Nope.

26:40.851 --> 26:42.311
Just the English speakers.

26:42.895 --> 26:44.354
We'll have to ask their permission.

26:44.438 --> 26:45.689
Fine. Ask.

26:46.773 --> 26:48.025
The sooner the better.

26:55.115 --> 26:58.660
Oh, shit. No, no, no, no, no, no.
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey. Hey. Hey!

26:58.744 --> 27:00.913
Are you there? Can you hear me?

27:00.996 --> 27:01.997
We can hear you.

27:04.583 --> 27:05.834
All five say yes.

28:01.306 --> 28:03.350
How you doin' back here, Carol?

28:03.433 --> 28:05.686
- Is there anything that we can get you?
- I'm good.

28:06.311 --> 28:07.312
Just...

28:09.898 --> 28:12.359
You're more than welcome
to sit up front with us, if you'd like.

28:12.442 --> 28:14.027
You could take the controls.

28:14.570 --> 28:15.863
It's fun.

28:15.946 --> 28:20.200
Who's flying this thing?
That gal from TGI Fridays?

28:21.034 --> 28:22.369
Maybe just concentrate on her.

28:24.162 --> 28:26.665
Well, let us know
if there's anything you need.

28:36.383 --> 28:40.387
Carol, this gathering today,
we have high hopes for it.

28:40.470 --> 28:41.471
Great.

28:42.723 --> 28:47.186
- But?
- But, as we say, your lives are your own.

28:49.021 --> 28:50.063
Which means what?

28:51.565 --> 28:53.567
We can't really protect you
from one another.

28:58.113 --> 29:00.407
We'll be landing in Bilbao in 40 minutes.

29:33.815 --> 29:35.526
- Where did you come from?
- Did you have to travel far?

29:35.609 --> 29:37.528
- Oh, yeah. I had a good time. Yes.
- Peru.

29:37.611 --> 29:39.112
- And you?
- China.

29:39.196 --> 29:41.198
I have some pictures. It's very beautiful.

29:45.953 --> 29:49.039
Yes. It's my first time
outside of my country.

29:50.916 --> 29:51.917
It was a bit long.

30:13.772 --> 30:16.859
Would it be acceptable
to everyone if we continue in English?

30:16.942 --> 30:17.943
- Yeah.
- Of course.

30:18.026 --> 30:19.361
- Sure.
- Wonderful.

30:21.947 --> 30:23.448
Sorry. I was just in the...

30:26.952 --> 30:27.995
Doesn't matter.

30:28.871 --> 30:29.872
Hi.

30:30.581 --> 30:32.958
Hi. I'm Carol.

30:33.834 --> 30:36.211
Hello. Otgonbayar.

30:36.920 --> 30:38.046
Pleased to meet you.

30:38.130 --> 30:39.339
Otgonbayar.

30:39.423 --> 30:42.134
- Otgonbayar.
- Otgonbayar. Okay. Pleased to meet you.

30:43.510 --> 30:45.846
My name is Xiu Mei. Hello.

30:45.929 --> 30:47.764
Hello, Xiu Mei.

30:47.848 --> 30:49.057
I'm Carol.

30:50.976 --> 30:52.269
Kusimayu.

30:52.352 --> 30:54.521
Kusimayu, that's a lovely name.

30:54.605 --> 30:56.607
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

30:57.232 --> 30:58.358
And...

30:59.484 --> 31:00.736
I'm Laxmi.

31:01.486 --> 31:02.487
Laxmi.

31:03.572 --> 31:06.408
Great to meet you.
Great to meet all of you.

31:08.994 --> 31:13.415
Wow. Just... Wow, right?

31:15.167 --> 31:16.335
This is such a relief.

31:25.552 --> 31:27.679
Do you know who these guys are?

31:27.763 --> 31:29.389
Hello, Carol.

31:29.473 --> 31:30.807
We're family members.

31:30.891 --> 31:33.727
This individual is Byamba,
Otgonbayar's daughter.

31:34.311 --> 31:38.941
Hi, Carol. This individual
is Neu Xiansheng, Xiu Mei's husband.

31:39.024 --> 31:41.527
T'ika, Kusimayu's aunt.

31:41.610 --> 31:43.737
Sisa, Kusimayu's cousin.

31:43.820 --> 31:45.781
Aarush, Laxmi's husband.

31:45.864 --> 31:48.825
Padma, mother of Laxmi. And this is...

31:48.909 --> 31:51.036
Ravi, Laxmi's nine-year-old son.

31:51.787 --> 31:53.705
We're very pleased to meet you, Carol.

31:55.707 --> 31:57.918
Yep. Yep, yep, yep.

31:58.001 --> 31:59.002
Yep.

32:03.340 --> 32:04.341
Wait a second.

32:04.424 --> 32:06.969
Including me, I thought there
was supposed to be six of us.

32:07.052 --> 32:08.428
I only count five.

32:09.179 --> 32:12.474
Number six is a gentleman from Mauritania.

32:12.558 --> 32:16.103
He requested a specific aircraft
which took a bit longer.

32:17.145 --> 32:21.149
Mister Koumba Diabaté invites you
aboard his plane once it arrives.

32:21.650 --> 32:24.069
He thinks it'll prove suitable
for your gathering.

32:55.642 --> 32:58.604
Hello, hello!

33:03.275 --> 33:04.693
Bienvenue à bord!

33:25.839 --> 33:27.716
It was available to whoever asked.

33:35.766 --> 33:38.018
Bonjour, enchanté.

33:38.101 --> 33:39.561
I am Koumba Diabaté.

33:39.645 --> 33:42.147
Bonjour. Carol Sturka. Nice plane.

33:44.274 --> 33:48.028
Je suis ravi de vous avoir à bord.

33:49.196 --> 33:50.989
Welcome to Spain, Mr. Diabaté.

33:51.073 --> 33:55.077
We hope your flight was most pleasant.

33:55.160 --> 33:57.746
How could it be otherwise?

33:58.080 --> 34:02.709
But please tell me,
what brings you aboard Air Force Koumba?

34:03.544 --> 34:05.587
She was available to whoever asked.

34:08.172 --> 34:09.800
Welcome aboard, Carol.

34:13.011 --> 34:14.554
This plane has upstairs.

34:18.934 --> 34:20.143
Yeah.

34:20.226 --> 34:25.815
This they call the "nuclear football."
With it, one could blow up the world.

34:27.317 --> 34:29.652
I am joking.
I do not think it works anymore.

34:29.735 --> 34:30.737
But don't drop it!

34:31.487 --> 34:32.489
Again, a joke.

34:32.572 --> 34:34.574
- Heavy.
- Which is fitting.

34:34.658 --> 34:37.286
Anything capable of blowing up the world
needs to have some heft to it,

34:37.369 --> 34:38.370
don't you think?

34:46.420 --> 34:48.005
Excuse me, excuse me.

34:49.505 --> 34:51.049
That was my first question to them.

34:51.550 --> 34:53.719
Hey, guys! Excuse me.

34:55.344 --> 34:56.346
Everyone?

34:57.222 --> 35:00.142
May we have your attention? Please?

35:03.187 --> 35:04.730
Thank you very much.

35:07.024 --> 35:09.735
So... I think we're all good here.

35:11.236 --> 35:16.408
Family members,
beautiful women, pirate lady.

35:16.491 --> 35:19.036
You can all just go wait out
on the tarmac.

35:21.747 --> 35:23.624
Why should my family have to leave?

35:23.707 --> 35:24.833
Yes, why?

35:24.917 --> 35:28.253
We need to talk
amongst ourselves, just the six of us.

35:28.337 --> 35:30.172
That's why we're here, right?

35:39.389 --> 35:40.682
Wait. Pirate lady.

35:40.766 --> 35:45.812
Are there any microphones in here
or recording devices?

35:45.896 --> 35:48.398
There's a built-in system
that came with the aircraft.

35:48.482 --> 35:50.108
We can make sure it's turned off.

35:57.449 --> 35:59.368
I did not know that was there.

35:59.451 --> 36:00.869
You have complete privacy.

36:01.495 --> 36:02.829
Call us if you need us.

36:20.389 --> 36:21.974
Actually, if you recall,

36:22.057 --> 36:24.059
Harrison Ford never rode in the escape pod

36:24.142 --> 36:25.853
which I thought was a clever gambit.

36:25.936 --> 36:27.980
- He stayed behind in the cargo hold.
- So,

36:28.063 --> 36:29.690
what are we gonna do about this?

36:35.946 --> 36:41.618
Anyone have any training in biology?
Or genetics?

36:45.706 --> 36:47.499
Anybody a doctor? A medical doctor?

36:50.794 --> 36:54.006
Any backgrounds in science? Of any kind?

36:58.886 --> 37:00.888
Anybody build a volcano?

37:10.898 --> 37:11.982
All right.

37:14.568 --> 37:15.819
I don't know how we do this.

37:17.196 --> 37:18.780
I don't know where we begin.

37:19.656 --> 37:20.657
But

37:21.742 --> 37:22.951
it's up to us now.

37:24.203 --> 37:26.747
The future of humanity is in our hands.

37:26.830 --> 37:29.666
As scary as that sounds, it is.

37:29.750 --> 37:33.170
It is up to us to put the world right.

37:41.303 --> 37:42.304
Why?

37:44.890 --> 37:46.725
Why save the world? Is that...

37:46.808 --> 37:48.685
Wait, is... That's your question?

37:48.769 --> 37:50.229
Why does the world need saving?

37:51.146 --> 37:53.649
At present, the situation seems very nice.

37:54.858 --> 37:57.569
Cool plane. Really.

37:58.320 --> 38:00.447
Meanwhile, everybody everywhere else

38:00.531 --> 38:03.867
has turned into some kind
of fucking pod person. Right?

38:03.951 --> 38:06.078
And it does not matter
how nice they are to us

38:06.161 --> 38:10.082
or how many supermodels they send
to peel our grapes and jerk us off,

38:10.165 --> 38:14.962
that does not
change the fact that this is not right.

38:15.045 --> 38:17.005
I've seen this movie.

38:17.965 --> 38:19.466
We've all seen this movie.

38:19.550 --> 38:21.635
And we know it does not end well.

38:22.678 --> 38:25.848
Are you the one who lost her temper
and made them all stop moving?

38:30.477 --> 38:33.188
When you did this, I was in an automobile.

38:33.772 --> 38:35.274
My grandfather was driving.

38:36.149 --> 38:39.361
The automobile crashed,
and my grandfather died.

38:43.240 --> 38:44.241
I'm...

38:45.951 --> 38:47.786
I'm sorry. I didn't...

38:47.870 --> 38:49.705
She not know they do that.

38:50.330 --> 38:51.582
Nobody know.

38:53.208 --> 38:55.252
And it won't happen again.

38:56.461 --> 38:58.338
I don't know. You seem very angry.

38:59.923 --> 39:02.050
I'm very sorry you lost your grandfather.

39:03.343 --> 39:05.554
But the rest of your family
waiting outside,

39:07.181 --> 39:08.765
you've lost them too.

39:09.766 --> 39:11.310
Everybody understands that, right?

39:11.393 --> 39:15.522
Your husbands, wives, parents, children...

39:15.606 --> 39:17.357
They're not them anymore.

39:17.441 --> 39:19.484
My child is still my child.

39:19.568 --> 39:20.611
Very much so.

39:20.694 --> 39:22.446
That cute little boy we just met?

39:22.529 --> 39:26.200
The one who can perform open-heart surgery
and fly the space shuttle?

39:26.283 --> 39:27.576
Yep, he's right as rain.

39:27.659 --> 39:29.077
You listen.

39:29.161 --> 39:30.829
That is my child out there.

39:30.913 --> 39:33.874
He is also your prime minister,

39:33.957 --> 39:37.794
some guy you dated in high school,
your gynecologist. Think about that.

39:37.878 --> 39:40.297
You... You are a horrible person.

39:40.380 --> 39:42.466
Okay, who is the angry one now? Hmm?

39:42.549 --> 39:44.676
Guys, I'm not looking for a fight here.

39:44.760 --> 39:47.387
I'm just trying to make
a point that this whole thing...

39:49.389 --> 39:50.849
We have to do something.

39:50.933 --> 39:52.142
Do what?

39:57.940 --> 40:00.651
I am not convinced
things are as bad as you say.

40:04.863 --> 40:08.325
As we speak,
no one is being robbed or murdered.

40:09.368 --> 40:10.661
No one is in prison.

40:12.037 --> 40:16.375
The color of one's skin, by all accounts,
now meaningless.

40:17.584 --> 40:21.088
All zoos are empty.
All dogs are off their chains.

40:23.674 --> 40:25.300
Peace on earth.

40:27.636 --> 40:29.221
Assuming that's even true...

40:31.181 --> 40:34.560
Ask yourselves what's been lost.

40:38.438 --> 40:39.982
Why zoos are empty?

40:40.065 --> 40:43.277
They emptied them. Everywhere.

40:43.360 --> 40:45.195
They let loose all the animal.

40:45.279 --> 40:47.823
Beijing Zoo is near my house.

40:48.448 --> 40:53.370
I look outside, I see giraffe
eat all the leaf off my tree.

40:53.453 --> 40:58.709
I say, "Shoo. Shoo. Go. Go."
It do not listen to me.

41:01.170 --> 41:06.341
I tell you this.
I do not give away my dog.

41:07.801 --> 41:10.762
Apparently,
when it came to the lions and the tigers,

41:10.846 --> 41:12.806
they suffered quite a few maulings.

41:12.890 --> 41:15.309
Can we just stick
with talking about the people?

41:17.603 --> 41:21.481
What's going to happen when they
figure out how to turn us into them?

41:23.609 --> 41:24.985
That is what I want.

41:26.904 --> 41:28.447
I want to be with my aunt.

41:28.530 --> 41:30.407
I want to be with my cousin.

41:31.366 --> 41:35.370
Oh, honey. No, you don't.
You may think you do, but you don't.

41:35.454 --> 41:36.580
Don't tell her how to think.

41:36.663 --> 41:39.249
Could you just... Please.

41:40.584 --> 41:41.585
Look,

41:42.920 --> 41:44.713
I know you are...

41:46.590 --> 41:51.094
lonely and scared and this whole thing...

41:53.388 --> 41:55.307
is terribly confusing.

41:57.935 --> 41:59.269
Believe me, I know.

42:01.271 --> 42:03.106
But everything about you that's you,

42:03.774 --> 42:08.195
everything that is personal
and individual and special...

42:08.278 --> 42:12.991
If we let this happen,
you won't have that anymore.

42:14.785 --> 42:16.870
I'll have it. I'll share it.

42:16.954 --> 42:18.247
What did they tell you?

42:19.164 --> 42:20.374
What kind of promises did they make?

42:20.457 --> 42:21.583
No promise.

42:22.251 --> 42:24.086
They only tell me what it's like.

42:25.504 --> 42:27.965
You don't think it sounds wonderful?

42:30.467 --> 42:32.135
You don't ask them what it's like?

42:32.928 --> 42:33.929
No.

42:34.012 --> 42:36.265
How could you not ask them what it's like?

42:36.348 --> 42:38.851
Raise your hand if you asked them.

42:41.019 --> 42:45.607
You sit there and you tell us
we must do this, we must do that.

42:45.691 --> 42:47.734
But you don't even
bother to educate yourself.

42:47.818 --> 42:50.112
Why should we listen to anything you say?

42:51.154 --> 42:54.074
Because I'm smart enough
to know you don't ask a drug dealer

42:54.157 --> 42:55.951
to describe their heroin.

42:56.618 --> 42:59.788
Now, what are we gonna do here?

43:00.497 --> 43:02.457
I'm open to suggestions.

43:08.589 --> 43:09.590
Who's hungry?

43:11.508 --> 43:13.719
I, myself, am famished.

43:21.643 --> 43:23.187
Hello, good people.

43:23.770 --> 43:26.481
We are interested in lunch!

43:42.706 --> 43:44.124
Voilà.

43:47.628 --> 43:48.629
Is this...

43:50.964 --> 43:52.674
Poulet Yassa!

43:54.301 --> 43:55.552
Incroyable.

44:01.517 --> 44:05.437
Exactly like my tantine Awa
made it when I was a child!

44:06.939 --> 44:09.024
However, and I'm not complaining mind you...

44:09.107 --> 44:10.609
I did order lobster.

44:10.692 --> 44:11.860
We apologize.

44:11.944 --> 44:16.782
We searched a wide radius, but the only
lobster currently available is live.

44:18.408 --> 44:20.118
We don't kill.

44:22.079 --> 44:23.622
Not even a lobster?

44:25.415 --> 44:29.086
Your chicken, fish, beef,
veggies are the freshest

44:29.169 --> 44:30.963
we could find in the local markets.

44:31.547 --> 44:33.423
We do hope you enjoy.

44:54.736 --> 44:56.530
So, you are vegetarian?

44:58.365 --> 45:00.117
That would be our preference, yes.

45:01.326 --> 45:03.161
What if I wanted escargot?

45:03.245 --> 45:05.080
Surely you can kill snails.

45:05.163 --> 45:06.373
No.

45:06.456 --> 45:07.916
A wasp even?

45:08.000 --> 45:11.587
If it's about to sting, you don't...

45:11.670 --> 45:12.671
kill it?

45:12.754 --> 45:13.755
No.

45:14.423 --> 45:16.258
What if you step on tiny...

45:17.551 --> 45:18.552
Insect.

45:18.635 --> 45:21.096
If you step on tiny insect by accident?

45:21.180 --> 45:22.639
We try not to.

45:22.723 --> 45:25.100
We can't purposely end life.

45:25.184 --> 45:26.393
It's not in our nature.

45:26.476 --> 45:30.606
Well, hip-fuckin'-hooray for you.

45:38.947 --> 45:42.659
They won't step on a bug,
but they'll enslave an entire planet.

45:43.452 --> 45:45.245
Yeah, that makes sense.

45:45.329 --> 45:48.999
Our joining is very much
the antithesis of slavery.

45:49.082 --> 45:50.584
If you're gonna hit me, hit me.

45:50.667 --> 45:51.668
Your "joining"?

45:52.586 --> 45:56.548
All the marketing brains on earth,
and that's what you came up with? Wow.

45:56.632 --> 45:58.884
There is a better word for it
in Celtiberian.

45:58.967 --> 46:01.887
Well, I don't remember you asking anyone.

46:02.804 --> 46:07.643
I don't recall anybody getting a vote
on whether or not they wanted a joining.

46:08.602 --> 46:10.479
We ourselves have no choice.

46:10.562 --> 46:12.856
For us, it's a biological imperative.

46:13.440 --> 46:14.733
Like breathing.

46:14.816 --> 46:19.780
But every time, one comes to understand
how wonderful it feels...

46:19.863 --> 46:23.325
How many fucking people died
during your wonderful fucking joining?

46:23.408 --> 46:25.827
Must you curse so much?

46:26.578 --> 46:28.247
There is a child present.

46:30.541 --> 46:31.875
I'm sorry, Ravi.

46:31.959 --> 46:32.960
I apologize.

46:33.043 --> 46:34.670
It's quite all right.

46:35.546 --> 46:36.964
Tell me, Ravi.

46:37.798 --> 46:42.511
For a pelvic exam, what kind of speculum
do you prefer, metal or plastic?

46:42.594 --> 46:43.595
What?

46:44.346 --> 46:46.139
It would depend.

46:46.890 --> 46:48.851
- Both have their uses.
- No, stop it.

46:48.934 --> 46:50.894
But, I mean, you probably
wouldn't do a palpation, right?

46:50.978 --> 46:52.646
You know,
not with those tiny little fingers.

46:52.729 --> 46:54.231
How dare you?

46:54.314 --> 46:55.983
How many people died?

46:56.066 --> 46:58.527
We didn't intend for anyone to die.

46:59.152 --> 47:01.405
And for the first month, no one did.

47:01.488 --> 47:06.076
We would bring in newcomers individually,
thousands every day.

47:06.159 --> 47:08.370
It was all very peaceful.

47:08.871 --> 47:10.706
But, then the military discovered us.

47:10.789 --> 47:14.209
And to avoid even more bloodshed,
we had to accelerate the process.

47:14.293 --> 47:15.752
So, how many?

47:19.339 --> 47:22.426
How many people died?

47:30.809 --> 47:36.815
886,477,591.

47:38.066 --> 47:39.943
As of this moment.

47:41.862 --> 47:43.655
Jesus Christ.

47:48.160 --> 47:49.161
Wow...

47:51.622 --> 47:53.373
I guess you gotta break a few eggs, huh?

47:56.627 --> 48:00.297
You killed 11 million.

48:14.603 --> 48:15.604
So...

48:17.731 --> 48:20.734
what if I caught a fish? Hmm?

48:20.817 --> 48:25.239
Or say I procured a chicken or a pig,
and I myself did the...

48:25.948 --> 48:27.157
What then?

48:30.077 --> 48:32.746
We would mourn the passing
of all these creatures.

48:34.414 --> 48:35.832
But you would cook them for me?

48:35.916 --> 48:37.042
Yes.

48:37.125 --> 48:38.252
Okay.

48:41.630 --> 48:44.216
Are you gonna let her continue like this?

48:46.093 --> 48:47.177
Carol.

48:47.261 --> 48:52.599
After lunch we were thinking you all
might like a tour of the Guggenheim.

48:53.308 --> 48:54.810
It's a beautiful museum.

48:54.893 --> 48:56.812
Frank Gehry designed it.

48:56.895 --> 48:58.522
Yeah, Helen talked about it.

48:58.605 --> 49:00.023
It was on our bucket list.

49:00.649 --> 49:02.276
But you already know that, don't you?

49:03.443 --> 49:04.778
All right.

49:04.862 --> 49:06.113
Warm up my plane.

49:06.196 --> 49:07.406
I'm going home.

49:07.948 --> 49:09.867
Good riddance.

49:23.297 --> 49:26.091
You, you, you, you...

49:27.801 --> 49:31.889
and especially you,
have the time of your lives.

49:33.015 --> 49:35.309
Enjoy it. Eat, drink and be merry.

49:35.392 --> 49:38.395
Go to the Guggenheim, Disneyland Paris,

49:38.478 --> 49:41.440
wherever else these whacked-out Moonies
take you next.

49:41.523 --> 49:44.902
But know this, you are traitors.

49:46.778 --> 49:50.324
You are traitors to the human race!

50:08.592 --> 50:09.593
Carol?

50:10.802 --> 50:12.179
Carol.

50:12.930 --> 50:14.806
Get off... Get off me.

50:15.807 --> 50:17.643
Get off me.

50:17.726 --> 50:21.063
Get the fuck off me! You fucking freaks!

50:21.146 --> 50:22.231
Get the fuck...

50:22.314 --> 50:24.024
Get off!

50:32.491 --> 50:35.452
God, no. No, no, no, no. No.

50:49.007 --> 50:50.217
Ravi?

50:50.300 --> 50:52.678
Ravi. Ravi.

52:12.883 --> 52:14.259
Good morning, Carol.

52:14.343 --> 52:15.761
We hope you slept well.

52:15.844 --> 52:17.346
How are you feeling?

52:19.556 --> 52:21.016
How are you feeling?

52:21.558 --> 52:23.060
We couldn't be better.

52:23.894 --> 52:25.187
Thank you for asking.

52:26.605 --> 52:28.774
May we get you anything?

52:33.529 --> 52:36.240
You got anything
to make me stop doing this?

52:37.324 --> 52:39.785
We don't. Sorry.

52:41.537 --> 52:43.163
But how about something to eat?

52:43.830 --> 52:46.834
We can make you some great bacon and eggs.

52:49.127 --> 52:53.632
Remember your trip to The Inn
at Little Washington, fall of 1998?

52:53.715 --> 52:57.094
They served that pepper bacon
you still talk about.

52:57.177 --> 52:59.012
We flew it in for you.

52:59.096 --> 53:01.557
And your favorite crispy brioche
from Les Crayères.

53:01.640 --> 53:05.519
How bad did I screw things up
with the other five?

53:08.397 --> 53:09.398
Did they leave?

53:11.733 --> 53:13.151
All but one.

53:40.429 --> 53:44.766
This is the finest martini
I have ever tasted.

53:53.483 --> 53:54.818
Good morning, Carol.

53:56.153 --> 53:57.154
Carol.

53:57.863 --> 53:58.864
How are you feeling?

54:01.033 --> 54:04.494
Better than I should for being
the biggest mass murderer since Stalin.

54:04.578 --> 54:07.497
I don't think these fine
people see it that way.

54:07.581 --> 54:09.041
No.

54:20.969 --> 54:23.138
Please, have a seat.

54:23.222 --> 54:25.265
Some coffee, perhaps?

54:34.191 --> 54:37.236
That Guggenheim is really worth a visit.

54:37.319 --> 54:39.029
Stunning architecture.

54:39.112 --> 54:40.447
You wanted to talk to me?

54:41.114 --> 54:42.115
Yes.

54:43.617 --> 54:46.245
I am headed to Las Vegas, Nevada.

54:46.328 --> 54:48.205
Have you been there?

54:48.288 --> 54:49.915
Looking for hotel recommendations?

54:49.998 --> 54:51.208
No, no, no, no.

54:51.291 --> 54:53.252
I am staying at The Westgate.

54:53.335 --> 54:56.713
I will occupy the penthouse
of Mr. Elvis Presley.

54:56.797 --> 54:58.590
Yeah, that sounds about right.

54:58.674 --> 55:00.592
Some say it is haunted by his ghost.

55:01.218 --> 55:02.386
This intrigues me.

55:02.886 --> 55:03.929
Okay.

55:04.513 --> 55:07.307
Well, give Elvis my regards.

55:07.391 --> 55:13.021
And, if it is acceptable to you
I wish for Zosia to accompany me.

55:14.356 --> 55:17.234
She suggested I ask.
I believe she needs your blessing.

55:17.317 --> 55:18.360
Who's Zosia?

55:19.862 --> 55:21.822
Your chaperone.

55:25.617 --> 55:27.369
Accompany you for what?

55:33.041 --> 55:34.835
Oh, Jesus Christ.

55:35.377 --> 55:37.546
I'm s... What can I say?

55:37.629 --> 55:41.008
In the past day, I've spent time with her,
gotten to know her.

55:41.675 --> 55:43.010
Learned her name.

55:43.886 --> 55:45.596
I feel we made a connection.

55:45.679 --> 55:46.889
Can I ask a question?

55:48.015 --> 55:51.810
What is wrong with you?

55:53.645 --> 55:55.439
Is it a medical condition?

55:55.522 --> 55:57.107
That it can't just...

55:57.191 --> 55:59.693
- stay in.
- I apologize.

55:59.776 --> 56:01.403
Clearly I have struck a nerve.

56:02.821 --> 56:04.072
If she is your companion...

56:04.156 --> 56:06.742
She's not my anything. None of them are.

56:06.825 --> 56:09.328
They are a bunch
of brain-damaged incompetents

56:09.411 --> 56:11.246
but you keep sticking your dick in them.

56:16.710 --> 56:19.671
Zosia, would you join us, please?

56:29.598 --> 56:31.683
Have I behaved in an untoward fashion?

56:32.476 --> 56:35.103
Have I shown you... any of you...

56:35.812 --> 56:40.275
affection that was in any way unwelcome?

56:42.444 --> 56:44.780
For us, affection is always welcome.

56:47.699 --> 56:52.913
Zosia, what is the square root of 46,279?

56:52.996 --> 56:54.540
Okay to round it off?

56:54.623 --> 56:56.583
Just a bit over 215.

56:57.167 --> 56:59.670
I have a strong sense that is correct.

56:59.753 --> 57:02.130
Okay. Let me see
if I've got this straight.

57:02.714 --> 57:06.552
Casanova McBoner here
wants you to join his harem,

57:06.635 --> 57:10.514
which is hunky-dory with you,
provided I give you my permission?

57:12.975 --> 57:14.685
That's your idea of paradise?

57:15.435 --> 57:17.813
- Being used like some sex doll?
- Hey.

57:17.896 --> 57:20.107
- And I'm what, your pimp?
- That is completely uncalled for.

57:20.190 --> 57:21.483
You're completely uncalled for.

57:21.567 --> 57:23.944
- The entire fucking world is ending...
- Carol.

57:24.027 --> 57:25.988
...and instead of doing the right thing
and trying to help me,

57:26.071 --> 57:28.907
- you'd rather run around, sticking your--
- Please! The last thing these people need

57:28.991 --> 57:31.159
is you losing your temper.

57:40.335 --> 57:43.922
You wanna go with him... go with him.

57:47.217 --> 57:49.344
Please, work this out yourselves.

57:50.721 --> 57:52.931
- We can't choose.
- Yes, you can.

57:53.473 --> 57:55.976
If you can do square roots in your head,
you can make choices.

57:56.894 --> 57:59.897
And there's a whole third option,
where you just tell us both to piss off.

58:02.399 --> 58:05.402
If we were to choose,
it would hurt one of you.

58:08.780 --> 58:09.990
We can't do that.

58:20.167 --> 58:22.878
Perhaps I have not seen
the movies you spoke of.

58:23.921 --> 58:28.717
But to me, this does not feel
like the end of the world.

58:39.311 --> 58:40.312
Ca--

01:00:07.441 --> 01:00:09.860
Stop! Open the door!
